<!DOCTYPE softwarelist SYSTEM "softwarelist.dtd">
<!--
license:CC0-1.0

    Roland SR-JV80 wave expansion boards, 8 MB each and 2 MB on the three
    Experience demo boards, taken as the mask ROM reads: nineteen address
    lines permuted within each 512 KB block and the eight data lines
    permuted, which is what the socket undoes.  The board carries its own
    label in the clear at offset 0 of the scrambled image, "Roland JV80 O.S."
    and then the sixteen-byte identity the host compares, once at the head of
    each of its 1 MB banks.

    Each entry is commented with that identity and with the build date the
    board stamps ten bytes after it, both read from the descrambled image.
    The year is that build date, which is what the images testify to rather
    than the date of sale.

    The Experience boards are Roland's own demonstration boards, which carry
    a demo's worth of waves and no title of their own.

    Not dumped: SR-JV80-20 (Ethnic Sound Collection), -21 (Concert Piano)
    and the regional and bundled boards.
-->

